  Summary: DEF-1 [NEW]. Checked specs/ first: DABSSmoothMinEscape covers SMOOTH-1, DABSSmoothReluPhantom covers SMOOTH-2, DABSGoodsRationing covers CLEAR-1, DABSInventoryStock covers INV-1, DABSAllocationExhaustive covers ALLOC-1, DABSSFCBalance covers SFC-1, DABSMoneyEndogenous covers MONEY-1. The two financial specs are the only candidates and neither covers DEF-1: DABSSFCBalance has a WriteOff posting but it is a bare principal cancellation with no seized-deposit recovery, no partition of the unpaid claim into recovery and loss, and no exit-rate cap at all; DABSMoneyEndogenous explicitly EXCLUDES write-offs from its scope because they break the narrower money identity. Neither carries a firm population, a liveness flag, or a per-quarter exit budget. So DEF-1 is genuinely uncovered. Wrote DABSDefaultLossConservation: a three-firm population with per-firm debt and deposit ledgers, a bank whose loan asset, deposit liability and capital are posted INDEPENDENTLY (never recomputed as assets minus liabilities), and a quarterly insolvency wave in which a DESIRED exit set from compute_default is filtered through the cap into a REALISED exit set. Each exit splits the unpaid claim exactly: recovery is the seized firm deposit capped at the claim, loss is the remainder, the bank asset is written down by the WHOLE claim while the deposit liability falls by the recovery and capital absorbs only the loss. Asserts loss conservation both per wave and cumulatively (recovery + loss = claim exactly, so no value is created or destroyed by an exit), recovery bounded by what the firm actually held, the realised exit rate within the cap against the ALIVE denominator, the cap binding exactly when desire exceeds it, deferral conserved as a residual, both ledger mirrors, balance-sheet closure in every reachable state, the loan stock and the capital stock reconstructed from their flows, dead firms holding no debt, and the population count reconciling against the exit counter. Two shadow ledgers give it the falsifiable bite: one debits capital by the full claim while still crediting the recovery, the double-count that destroys the recovered value twice, pinned to sit exactly cumRecovery below the true capital and to break closure the moment anything is recovered; the other cancels the firm's debt without writing down the bank asset, the one-sided write-off that leaves the bank carrying claims against firms that no longer exist, pinned to exceed the true loan stock by exactly everything ever written off. SMOOTH-1 [COVERED] by DABSSmoothMinEscape, SMOOTH-2 [COVERED] by DABSSmoothReluPhantom, CLEAR-1 [COVERED] by DABSGoodsRationing, INV-1 [COVERED] by DABSInventoryStock, ALLOC-1 [COVERED] by DABSAllocationExhaustive, SFC-1 [COVERED] by DABSSFCBalance, MONEY-1 [COVERED] by DABSMoneyEndogenous. Remaining checklist items (SCHED-1, PARAM-1) untouched.
